        "date": "2026-11-11T09:02:16Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(app,ui): built-in 5-axis self-centering vises, centred on the stock\n\nSelf-centering vises at 52, 75, 80 and 125 mm jaw width ride #788's\nbuilt-in vise as a style (`ViseStyle::SelfCentering`): both jaws close on\nthe centre, so \"Fit to the stock\" centres the vise on the stock and\ncloses the jaws to its width within the clamping range. The geometry is\none generated closed shell (body, two jaw bodies, an optional dovetail\nlip drawn solid). Nonsense figures, stock outside the clamping range and\nstock off the vise's centre are refused by name. Placing and editing are\nthe existing InsertVise / SetVise (one undo each); the project file takes\nan optional `self_centering` key; MCP `add_builtin_vise` / `set_vise`\nlist the sizes and take min_opening / lip_height / lip_depth; the dialog\nshows the sizes in their own row with their own fields.\n\nTilted setups: the placed vise is judged by the posed mesh laws - a tool\nleaning into a jaw is struck where the same tip upright clears it, the\nsame lean from the centre clears, and a 3+2 face over the clamped stock\nposts until the jaws are raised into it.\n\nFixes #787\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
